<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong accountants elect top officials.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong accountants elect top officials.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Society of Accountants said it had elected Tim T.L. Lui as president and Aloysius H.Y. Tse and P.M. Kam as vice presidents during its annual general meeting on Friday.</p>
<p>Lui replaces outgoing president T. Brian Stevenson.</p>
<p>Lui is a partner at Coopers &amp; Lybrand, Tse is a partner at KPMG Peat Marwick and Kam is group financial controller of Jardine Matheson Ltd, the 11,500-member society said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
